error[keywords]: `int32` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
   ┌ test.idl:2:8
   │
 2 │ struct int32 {  // 'int32' is a primitive type keyword
   ·        ^^^^^ this is an IDL keyword
 3 │     long value;
 4 │ };
   └──
 help: the keyword can be escaped by changing to `_int32`
 note: keywords are matched case-insensitively against identifiers
